docs: correct stale permission claims and stop the version drift

The user spotted `dynamicCordisRunner/*` listed among endpoints "closed to
every role". Checking the built artifact, `full` actually holds 12 of those
endpoints and isNeverDelegated() returns false for them -- the doc has been
wrong since 0.3.2 moved them out of the red lines.

Corrected in every place that carried the claim:

- README/A: section 5 no longer lists dynamicCordisRunner as closed; it now
  states it is full-only, and remoteAccess/follow + $events are named as the
  actually-closed ones. The "red lines are never delegated" bullet dropped
  dynamicCordisRunner and pluginInventory, the latter because
  pluginInventory/list is open to all three roles and has been for a while.
- DESIGN.md: the full role now names the dynamic-execution surface and the two
  directoryPicker endpoints it exclusively holds.
- render-api-matrix.mjs: the generated table claimed full is denied plugin
  install and dynamic execution -- the exact opposite of the code. Fixed, and
  the matrix regenerated.

Separately, docs/DEPLOY.md still declared "current version 0.3.4" long after
the bump. release-check only validated README, README.en and DESIGN, so the
drift went unnoticed. DEPLOY is now in versionedDocs; deliberately re-breaking
it fails the check with a precise message.

Verified: typecheck, build, all five gates and release-check 14/14 pass.
